      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُوَيْدَآءُ</span></b>  dim. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُوْدَآءُ</span>, fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْوَدُ</span>, q. v.: (Mgh:)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَوَادٌ</span>, in two places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُوَيْدٌ</span>: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4- 
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْوَدُ</span>, near the end of the paragraph. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  Also
<i>A certain bird.</i> (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b6-  <i>And Salt tracts</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِبَاخ</span>)
of [plants of the kind called] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَجِيل</span>: Kr explains
it by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِبْتَةٌ</span> [app. a mistranscription for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَبْتَةٌ</span> <i>a
plant</i>]; without describing it. (M.)

